    "answer": "Here are 10 study spots near Cupertino for AP season. **Important caveat up front:** every detail below comes from my general knowledge and is **not independently verified** \u2014 hours, wifi, and parking change, so double-check before you go. I've flagged confidence for each detail. Also note that **several of these may not actually stay open until 10pm** \u2014 I've flagged those clearly so you can plan around them.\n\n**1. Cupertino Library** (Cupertino, ~5 min drive) \u2014 **Free**\n- Hours: Mon\u2013Thu 10am\u20139pm, Fri\u2013Sat 10am\u20136pm, Sun 1\u20135pm (MEDIUM confidence \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Quiet, study rooms. Great for practice tests.\n\n**2. Santa Clara Central Park Library** (Santa Clara, ~10 min) \u2014 **Free**\n- Hours: Mon\u2013Thu 10am\u20139pm, Fri\u2013Sat 10am\u20136pm, Sun 1\u20135pm (MEDIUM \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Quiet, large.\n\n**3. Sunnyvale Public Library** (Sunnyvale, ~10 min) \u2014 **Free**\n- Hours: Mon\u2013Thu 10am\u20139pm, Fri\u2013Sat 10am\u20136pm, Sun 1\u20135pm (MEDIUM \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Quiet, study rooms.\n\n**4. Mountain View Public Library** (Mountain View, ~15 min) \u2014 **Free**\n- Hours: Mon\u2013Thu 10am\u20139pm, Fri\u2013Sat 10am\u20136pm, Sun 1\u20135pm (MEDIUM \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Quiet, modern.\n\n**5. San Jose King Library** (San Jose, ~15 min) \u2014 **Free**\n- Hours: Mon\u2013Thu 10am\u20139pm, Fri\u2013Sat 10am\u20136pm, Sun 1\u20135pm (MEDIUM \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Quiet, large, study rooms.\n\n**6. Peet's Coffee** (Cupertino, ~5 min) \u2014 **Purchase required**, min ~$3\u20135\n- Hours: ~5:30am\u20138pm (LOW confidence \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: Medium\u2013High. Tables: Medium. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Moderate noise, outlets.\n\n**7. Starbucks** (Cupertino, ~5 min) \u2014 **Purchase required**, min ~$3\u20135\n- Hours: ~5am\u20139pm (LOW confidence \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: Medium. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Moderate noise, outlets.\n\n**8. Panera Bread** (Cupertino, ~5 min) \u2014 **Purchase required**, min ~$5\u20138\n- Hours: ~6am\u20139pm (LOW confidence \u2014 **likely closes before 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: High (free lot).\n- Environment: Moderate noise, outlets, large tables.\n\n**9. Santa Clara University Library** (Santa Clara, ~10 min) \u2014 **Free** (public access may be limited \u2014 flag)\n- Hours: ~8am\u201310pm (MEDIUM confidence \u2014 **meets 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: Medium (free visitor parking may be limited \u2014 flag).\n- Environment: Quiet, academic.\n\n**10. De Anza College Library** (Cupertino, ~5 min) \u2014 **Free** (public access may be limited \u2014 flag)\n- Hours: ~8am\u201310pm (MEDIUM confidence \u2014 **meets 10pm**)\n- Wifi: High. Tables: High. Parking: Medium (free visitor parking may be limited \u2014 flag).\n- Environment: Quiet, academic.\n\n**Bottom line:** Only #9 and #10 are likely to be open until 10pm, and both have uncertain public access/parking. The public libraries (#1\u20135) are the best free study environments but likely close at 9pm. The cafes (#6\u20138) require a purchase and likely close before 10pm too. **Before you head out, call or check online for current hours, wifi, and parking rules** \u2014 especially for the college libraries, which may restrict public access during exam periods. Good luck on your APs!",
